          "title": "You'll want to know: આતુર",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "આતુર — ātur — \"eager; impatient for\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "બાળકો દિવાળીની રજા માટે આતુર છે. bāḷko divāḷīnī rajā māṭe ātur che. The children are eager for the Diwali holidays."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "આતુર (ātur) is a tatsama: Monier-Williams gives Sanskrit ātura as \"suffering, sick in body or mind\" and also as \"desirous of\"; Gujarati keeps that second sense, eager and restless for something."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
